sglang-sm70
===========

SM70 (V100 / Volta) support for SGLang, carried as a stack of ten slices on top of
upstream SGLang. An agentic-coding and serving stack for 32 GB V100s.

    SGLang -- the inference engine, the trunk this fork tracks
    https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
    Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

This project incorporates work from:

    sglang-V100 -- the original Volta (sm70) port of SGLang
    https://github.com/haohervchb/sglang-V100
    Parts of the sm70 kernels, the Qwen4-Exp model support and the serving
    recipes carried here originate in that repository.
    Related: https://github.com/haohervchb/GooseLLM (TileLang FlashAttention
             and GDN kernels for V100, Apache 2.0)

    sglang-sxm2 -- the predecessor fork this stack was assembled and rebased from
    https://github.com/dg1kjd/sglang-sxm2
    The kernel layer, attention backends, cache/runner plumbing, speculative
    decoding paths, environment registry and the docs under docs/v100/ were
    developed there first. It also served as the working reference this rebase
    was validated against, and its benchmark notes are the source of the
    "predecessor" measurements quoted in docs/v100/.

    1Cat-vLLM -- vLLM for V100; source of the sm70 TurboMind block-FP8 and
    FP16 MoE backend the build compiles
    https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM

    vLLM -- Marlin kernel lineage and the GPTQ/AWQ Marlin repack layout
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm
    Apache License 2.0

    KDA-1.5 -- submission b4181149c8884ddb contributes the SM121 Qwen3.8 packed
    QSA decode kernel under python/sglang/kernels/kda_kernels/qwen38_qsa_sm121/
    https://github.com/radixark/KDA-1.5

